Goemon's Great Adventure (Nintendo 64) - decompilation changelog
Newest entry on top.

2026-10-26
- Building after an update: build_rom.py now splits the ROM again when goemonsgreatadv.yaml is newer than the
  linker script made from it. Before, a checkout updated across a change to the yaml kept linking the old segments
  and stopped on a missing C file (src/tlb/tlb_0184.c, for one). A fresh clone was never affected. Checked: an
  older checkout updated this way builds to both SHA-1s with plain build_rom.py.
- A bug of the original game, documented where it is (`//! @bug`, src/tlb/tlb_0198.c): the merchant in the town,
  by the lizard man's house, walks in place against a wall, on a real N64 too. His route only turns him to face
  180 degrees and loops; townspeople start out playing their walk, and nothing in his route sets a standing
  animation. Found while porting the game, by reading his state live off a 3DS. The decomp keeps the game's bytes.

2026-10-20
- First public release. Every function and every data block of the US ROM is C that builds to
  both of the ROM's SHA-1s (the decompressed ROM's and the shipped ROM's), with real names, the
  assets in real formats (PNG, model and table C, scenario text, audio banks), and one prototype
  per function in its module's header. canon-decompilation-tools/README.md tells how to build
  it and what each tool does. Earlier history is kept privately.
